"""
CRENEL v0.5.0 - build hook.  Emits crenel_pkg.vhd (pure Python, no dependencies).

The tables were fitted to the source photo (WIN_20230223_01_46_41) in .heirloom_work/rb_crenel
(proto.py, tables.py, mkhook.py) and are carried here as data:

  C_CY / C_CU / C_CV  2048 x 8: the colour ROM, address = palette(2) & class(3) & level(6).
           Classes: 0 navy ground ramp (B 50 + 2 level), 1 / 2 / 3 pink fills (upper bar purple,
           lower magenta, lower tooth / V / blocks) running to the hot-pink ridge (level 0 = the
           dark undershoot, 1 = plain fill, 32 = the rim), 4 the echo lines, 5 the arch ring by its
           radial offset, 6 the camera colouriser (navy -> blue with ripple folds and the green /
           red fringes), 7 navy.  Palettes: Photo, Ember, Jade, Rust (hue rotations of the photo).
           Y and chroma are 10-bit / 4, U/V in the hardware convention (U = Cr), luma pre-boosted by
           16/13 so the output luma scale (white -> ~777) lands the photo's levels.
  C_LR     1024 x 16, the per-line engine's table: 0..539 the tile phase increment 2^24/T(y) every
           second virtual line (the measured FM bend and the slips), 544..671 the crenel ridge
           chevron by |y - 151|, 672..799 ridge amplitude / near-bar echo class by |y - 151|, 800..911 the
           dome half-width (tile phase) by y - 300, 928..982 the arcs' bow by y - 645, 992..1023
           the tooth corner roundings and fillets (crenel phase), 912..927 the dash-row hashes.
  C_RID / C_ECH / C_GLO / C_WOB  small per-pixel profiles: ridge, echo line, blue glow, arc wobble.
  C_SQ     256 x 16 squares (the arch ring's radius).  C_EGL  echo gain by K3 (square law).
  C_ECP    1024 x 8 echo-line profiles (2 feedback echoes + the dim zone) by near-bar class and distance.
"""
